{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.eos_borromean_cfl","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.eos_borromean_cfl","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.eos_borromean_cfl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.eos_borromean_cfl","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/eos_borromean_cfl.lean#L50-L161","doc":"**Manuscript statement** (full body):\n\n**Proposition.**\nLet $q > 1$ be the substrate parameter, $\\hbar_q = (q-1)/q$,\nand $V_B = 7.32772$ the Borromean volume.  The two topological\nphases of dense quark matter have distinct equations of state:\n\n**1. Borromean phase** (confined hadronic matter, $\\rho < \\rho_c$).\n\nThe baryon mass is $M_B = V_B / \\hbar_q^2$.  For a cold,\ndegenerate Fermi gas of baryons at number density $n_B$, the\nenergy density and pressure are\n\n$$\n  \\varepsilon_B(n_B)\n  = \n  M_B  n_B\n  + \n  \\frac{3}{5}\n  \\frac{\\hbar_q^2(3\\pi^2)^{2/3}}{2M_B}\n   n_B^{5/3},\n$$\n\n$$\n  P_B(n_B)\n  = \n  \\frac{\\hbar_q^2(3\\pi^2)^{2/3}}{5M_B}\n   n_B^{5/3}.\n$$\n\nThe speed of sound in the Borromean phase is\n\n$$\n  c_{s,B}^2\n  = \n  \\frac{dP_B}{d\\varepsilon_B}\n  = \n  \\frac{2}{3}\n  \\frac{E_F}{M_B + E_F}\n$$\n\nwhere $E_F = \\hbar_q^2(3\\pi^2 n_B)^{2/3} / (2M_B)$ is the\nFermi energy.  Since $M_B \\gg E_F$ at nuclear densities:\n$c_{s,B}^2 \\ll 1$ (non-relativistic regime).\n\n**2. CFL phase** (color superconducting, $\\rho > \\rho_c$).\n\nThe effective quark mass is $M_D = \\frac{1}{3}(q + q^{-1})$\n(crossing energy per quark, no volume contribution since\n$\\mathrm{Vol}(\\mathcal{L}_H) = 0$).  For a degenerate quark\nFermi gas at quark number density $n_q = 3 n_B$, the energy\ndensity includes the CFL gap contribution:\n\n$$\n  \\varepsilon_D(n_B)\n  = \n  3M_D n_B\n  + \n  \\frac{3}{5}\n  \\frac{\\hbar_q^2(3\\pi^2)^{2/3}}{2M_D}\n   (3 n_B)^{5/3}\n  - \n  \\frac{3\\Delta_{\\mathrm{CFL}}^2 \\mu_q^2}{\\pi^2},\n$$\n\n$$\n  P_D(n_B)\n  = \n  \\frac{\\hbar_q^2(3\\pi^2)^{2/3}}{5M_D}\n   (3 n_B)^{5/3}\n  + \n  \\frac{3\\Delta_{\\mathrm{CFL}}^2 \\mu_q^2}{\\pi^2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mu_q = \\hbar_q(3\\pi^2 n_q)^{1/3}/(2M_D)^{1/2}$ is\nthe quark chemical potential and\n$\\Delta_{\\mathrm{CFL}} = q + q^{-1}$ is the gap\n([Hopf diquark](#def:hopf-diquark)).\n\n**3. Stiffness ratio.**  The ratio of pressures at equal baryon\ndensity is\n\n$$\n  \\frac{P_D}{P_B}\n  = \n  \\frac{M_B}{M_D} \\cdot 3^{5/3}\n  + \n  \\frac{3\\Delta_{\\mathrm{CFL}}^2 \\mu_q^2}{\\pi^2 P_B}.\n$$\n\nThe first term gives the dominant contribution.  At\n$q =\n\n[…truncated; see manuscript for remainder…]\n\n    The proposition is **named** below as a `def … : Prop` (pattern C):\n    the energy densities, pressures and chemical potential are opaque\n    many-body inputs, so the three-part EOS claim is recorded as the\n    conditional conjecture over the context rather than discharged by a\n    fake projection. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:eos-borromean-cfl","label":"prop:eos-borromean-cfl","md":"quantum-observable-universe/observations/eos-borromean-cfl.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.μ_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.μ_q","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/eos_borromean_cfl.lean#L48-L48","doc":"Quark chemical potential `μ_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.hbar_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.hbar_q","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/eos_borromean_cfl.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Substrate `ℏ_q = (q − 1)/q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.Δ_CFL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.Δ_CFL","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/eos_borromean_cfl.lean#L44-L44","doc":"CFL gap `Δ_CFL = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.P_D","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.P_D","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/eos_borromean_cfl.lean#L42-L42","doc":"The CFL-phase pressure `P_D(n_B)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.ε_D","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.ε_D","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/eos_borromean_cfl.lean#L40-L40","doc":"The CFL-phase energy density `ε_D(n_B)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.P_B","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.P_B","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/eos_borromean_cfl.lean#L38-L38","doc":"The Borromean-phase pressure `P_B(n_B)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.ε_B","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.ε_B","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/eos_borromean_cfl.lean#L36-L36","doc":"The Borromean-phase energy density `ε_B(n_B)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.n_B","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.n_B","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/eos_borromean_cfl.lean#L34-L34","doc":"Baryon number density `n_B`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.M_D","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.M_D","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/eos_borromean_cfl.lean#L32-L32","doc":"CFL effective quark mass. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.M_B","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.M_B","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/eos_borromean_cfl.lean#L30-L30","doc":"Borromean baryon mass. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.q","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/eos_borromean_cfl.lean#L28-L28","doc":"Substrate parameter `q : ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/eos_borromean_cfl.lean#L26-L26","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EosBorromeanCflContext","kind":"class","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/eos_borromean_cfl.lean#L23-L48","doc":"Abstract context (inputs) for the `eos_borromean_cfl` claim — the\nsubstrate parameter, the two phase masses, the densities, pressures,\ngap and chemical potential.  No field asserts a conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0}]}